From b775e499b8214e3256754e22634b8acc6d1fed2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cosmo <forhchs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:41:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add standalone 5-player arena runner and fix upstream
 game bugs

src/arena: seeded role/seat shuffles, per-game JSONL event logs, async
runner with retry and per-game resume, sharding, and three model
backends: claude_cli (Claude Code headless on the user's own login),
anthropic (Claude API key), and an offline fake model. The search
agent's planner routes through the same backends.

Fixes to existing code:
- engine.from_presets stored game state on the class, so concurrent
  games shared roles
- the search planner's actor enumerator ignored default_player_order,
  so it reasoned as the lowest-numbered acting player; discussion used
  the quest leader's private information
- MultiAgentProxy labelled seat i as "Player i+1" in broadcast
  discussion, misattributing every line
- search agent RNG was hard-coded to seed 12
- langchain/tiktoken imports made lazy so the arena runs without them

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U1d3PHHyK6qXqb43QY1Yf6
